{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b9ba2a8497a30d76", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# QuarkAudio Technical Report\narXiv: 2512.20151\nAuthors: Chengwei Liu, Haoyin Yan, Shaofei Xue, Xiaotao Liang, Xiaofu Chen, Bin Gong, Zheng Xue, Gang Song\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: codec_vae\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We present H-Codec, a unified discrete audio tokenizer that integrates self-supervised learning representations into the tokenization process via dual-stream (acoustic and semantic) quantization, achieving remarkable audio reconstruction quality at a low frame rate.\n  2. We introduce advanced H-Codec variants, including H-Codec-1.5 with a dynamic frame-rate mechanism for adaptive temporal resolution and H-Codec-2.0 extending the sampling rate to 48 kHz for higher fidelity.\n  3. We propose QuarkAudio, a unified decoder-only autoregressive language model framework that uses task-specific conditional information and special task tokens to distinguish and unify multiple audio processing and generation tasks within a single set of shared weights.\n  4. We extend unified audio generation to universal free-form audio editing guided by natural language instructions, covering both speech semantic editing and audio event editing.\n  5. We demonstrate that QuarkAudio achieves competitive or comparable high-fidelity generation performance against state-of-the-art task-specific or multi-task systems across speech restoration, target speaker extraction, speech separation, voice conversion, and language-queried audio source separation tasks.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/功能-语音编辑, TTS/功能-多任务统一, 压缩, 压缩/量化-RVQ, 压缩/语义声学-语义, 压缩/语义声学-声学\n===\n# WavLM: Large-Scale Self-Supervised Pre-Training for Full Stack Speech Processing\narXiv: 2110.13900\nAuthors: Sanyuan Chen, Chengyi Wang, Zhengyang Chen, Yu Wu, Shujie Liu, Zhuo Chen, Jinyu Li, Naoyuki Kanda, Takuya Yoshioka, Xiong Xiao, Jian Wu, Long Zhou, Shuo Ren, Yanmin Qian, Yao Qian, Jian Wu, Michael Zeng, Xiangzhan Yu, Furu Wei\nYear: 2021 | Venue: \nTopic: speech_representation\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. WavLM introduces a general pre-trained model for full stack speech processing tasks, moving beyond the focus on specific task groups like ASR in prior self-supervised learning works.\n  2. A masked speech denoising and prediction framework is proposed to jointly learn speech content modeling and denoising, effectively improving performance on non-ASR tasks such as speaker verification, diarization, and separation.\n  3. Gated relative position bias is integrated into the Transformer structure to adaptively adjust relative position biases based on current speech content, enhancing sequence ordering capture and ASR performance.\n  4. The self-supervised speech pre-training data is scaled up to 94k hours from diverse domains, alleviating audiobook data bias and improving model robustness.\n  5. State-of-the-art results are achieved on the SUPERB benchmark and representative benchmarks for speaker verification, speech separation, and speaker diarization, with models and code publicly released.\n\nTags: SSL, ASR, SSL/预测式-离散\n===\n# AISHELL6-whisper: A Chinese Mandarin Audio-visual Whisper Speech Dataset with Speech Recognition Baselines\narXiv: 2509.23833\nAuthors: Cancan Li, Fei Su, Juan Liu, Hui Bu, Yulong Wan, Hongbin Suo, Ming Li\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: speech_dataset\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We present AISHELL6-Whisper, the largest open-source Chinese Mandarin audio-visual whisper speech dataset featuring 30 hours each of parallel whisper and normal speech with synchronized frontal facial videos.\n  2. We propose an audio-visual speech recognition baseline based on the Whisper-Flamingo framework that integrates a parallel training strategy to align embeddings across speech types.\n  3. We introduce a lightweight projection layer specifically designed to adapt the model to whisper speech's spectral properties and bridge the acoustic gap with normal speech.\n  4. Our proposed model achieves a Character Error Rate of 4.13% for whisper speech and 1.11% for normal speech on the AISHELL6-Whisper test set.\n  5. Our approach establishes new state-of-the-art results on the public wTIMIT benchmark, demonstrating strong cross-lingual transferability.\n\nTags: ASR, ASR/训练-SSL微调, ASR/训练-监督", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "caaae97e-a19c-4b90-8f0d-70cb62ba1a44", "uuid": "e4e610a2-4c25-4a28-b1db-a1ff97ed6d6d", "timestamp": "2026-08-11T07:25:17.237Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# QuarkAudio Technical Report\narXiv: 2512.20151\nAuthors: Chengwei Liu, Haoyin Yan, Shaofei Xue, Xiaotao Liang, Xiaofu Chen, Bin Gong, Zheng Xue, Gang Song\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: codec_vae\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We present H-Codec, a unified discrete audio tokenizer that integrates self-supervised learning representations into the tokenization process via dual-stream (acoustic and semantic) quantization, achieving remarkable audio reconstruction quality at a low frame rate.\n  2. We introduce advanced H-Codec variants, including H-Codec-1.5 with a dynamic frame-rate mechanism for adaptive temporal resolution and H-Codec-2.0 extending the sampling rate to 48 kHz for higher fidelity.\n  3. We propose QuarkAudio, a unified decoder-only autoregressive language model framework that uses task-specific conditional information and special task tokens to distinguish and unify multiple audio processing and generation tasks within a single set of shared weights.\n  4. We extend unified audio generation to universal free-form audio editing guided by natural language instructions, covering both speech semantic editing and audio event editing.\n  5. We demonstrate that QuarkAudio achieves competitive or comparable high-fidelity generation performance against state-of-the-art task-specific or multi-task systems across speech restoration, target speaker extraction, speech separation, voice conversion, and language-queried audio source separation tasks.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/功能-语音编辑, TTS/功能-多任务统一, 压缩, 压缩/量化-RVQ, 压缩/语义声学-语义, 压缩/语义声学-声学\n===\n# WavLM: Large-Scale Self-Supervised Pre-Training for Full Stack Speech Processing\narXiv: 2110.13900\nAuthors: Sanyuan Chen, Chengyi Wang, Zhengyang Chen, Yu Wu, Shujie Liu, Zhuo Chen, Jinyu Li, Naoyuki Kanda, Takuya Yoshioka, Xiong Xiao, Jian Wu, Long Zhou, Shuo Ren, Yanmin Qian, Yao Qian, Jian Wu, Michael Zeng, Xiangzhan Yu, Furu Wei\nYear: 2021 | Venue: \nTopic: speech_representation\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. WavLM introduces a general pre-trained model for full stack speech processing tasks, moving beyond the focus on specific task groups like ASR in prior self-supervised learning works.\n  2. A masked speech denoising and prediction framework is proposed to jointly learn speech content modeling and denoising, effectively improving performance on non-ASR tasks such as speaker verification, diarization, and separation.\n  3. Gated relative position bias is integrated into the Transformer structure to adaptively adjust relative position biases based on current speech content, enhancing sequence ordering capture and ASR performance.\n  4. The self-supervised speech pre-training data is scaled up to 94k hours from diverse domains, alleviating audiobook data bias and improving model robustness.\n  5. State-of-the-art results are achieved on the SUPERB benchmark and representative benchmarks for speaker verification, speech separation, and speaker diarization, with models and code publicly released.\n\nTags: SSL, ASR, SSL/预测式-离散\n===\n# AISHELL6-whisper: A Chinese Mandarin Audio-visual Whisper Speech Dataset with Speech Recognition Baselines\narXiv: 2509.23833\nAuthors: Cancan Li, Fei Su, Juan Liu, Hui Bu, Yulong Wan, Hongbin Suo, Ming Li\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: speech_dataset\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We present AISHELL6-Whisper, the largest open-source Chinese Mandarin audio-visual whisper speech dataset featuring 30 hours each of parallel whisper and normal speech with synchronized frontal facial videos.\n  2. We propose an audio-visual speech recognition baseline based on the Whisper-Flamingo framework that integrates a parallel training strategy to align embeddings across speech types.\n  3. We introduce a lightweight projection layer specifically designed to adapt the model to whisper speech's spectral properties and bridge the acoustic gap with normal speech.\n  4. Our proposed model achieves a Character Error Rate of 4.13% for whisper speech and 1.11% for normal speech on the AISHELL6-Whisper test set.\n  5. Our approach establishes new state-of-the-art results on the public wTIMIT benchmark, demonstrating strong cross-lingual transferability.\n\nTags: ASR, ASR/训练-SSL微调, ASR/训练-监督", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
